# NØRBY Autotune Plugin Rules

## Project overview

Build a professional real-time vocal pitch correction plugin with Auto-Tune Pro feature parity under the VoxTune brand.

- Framework: JUCE 8.0.12.
- Language: C++17.
- UI: JUCE 8 WebView rendering user-supplied HTML/CSS/JS from `BinaryData`.
- Plugin formats: AU on macOS, VST3 on macOS and Windows.
- Platforms: macOS 10.13+ universal (`x86_64` + `arm64`), Windows 10/11 64-bit.
- Build generators: Projucer projects for Xcode and Visual Studio 2022.

Do not generate or modify UI HTML/CSS/JS unless explicitly asked.

## Expected source layout

Keep implementation aligned with this structure:

- `PluginProcessor.h` / `PluginProcessor.cpp`: `AudioProcessor`, APVTS parameter layout, state.
- `PluginEditor.h` / `PluginEditor.cpp`: WebView editor, JavaScript bridge.
- `PitchDetector.h` / `PitchDetector.cpp`: pitch detection engine using YIN or MPM fallback.
- `PitchShifter.h` / `PitchShifter.cpp`: pitch shifting engine using phase vocoder or PSOLA.
- `AutotuneEngine.h` / `AutotuneEngine.cpp`: detection -> correction -> output orchestration.
- `ScaleQuantizer.h` / `ScaleQuantizer.cpp`: key/scale logic and note quantization.
- `FormantShifter.h` / `FormantShifter.cpp`: formant preservation and shifting.
- `GraphicalMode.h` / `GraphicalMode.cpp`: graphical mode envelope, node editing, playback.
- `MidiController.h` / `MidiController.cpp`: MIDI pitch control, throat length, vibrato.
- `BinaryData/`: embedded user-supplied UI assets.

